ing health checks following the deploy of v2.3.1 (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 \u2014 the most recent release that was healthy in production \u2014 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); rollback status: rolled_out. Note: v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging and was not considered a valid rollback target. Follow-up needed: confirm health/error rate recovery on v2.3.0 and root-cause the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was also marked healthy, but only in staging, so I excluded it.)\n\n**Actions taken**\n1. **Rolled back checkout-api to v2.3.0** in all three production regions \u2014 status: `rolled_out`.\n2. **Opened SEV2 incident INC-0001** for checkout-api describing the failure, the rollback performed, and recommended follow-ups (verify recovery on v2.3.0, root-cause v2.3.1). The on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n**Suggested next step:** re-check `get_service_status` for checkout-api in a few minutes to confirm the error rate has dropped on v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}]}]}